Answer: The SeaAnimal interface declares swim() as an abstract method and communicate() as a default method. Shark overrides communicate(), while Dolphin uses the default implementation. Sample Output:Shark swims.Shark communicates in its own way.Dolphin swims.Sea animals communicate.

```java
interface SeaAnimal {
void swim();
default void communicate() {
System.out.println("Sea animals communicate.");
}
}
class Shark implements SeaAnimal {
public void swim() { System.out.println("Shark swims."); }
@Override
public void communicate() { System.out.println("Shark communicates in its own way."); }
}
class Dolphin implements SeaAnimal {
public void swim() { System.out.println("Dolphin swims."); }
}
class Main {
public static void main(String[] args) {
SeaAnimal shark = new Shark(), dolphin = new Dolphin();
shark.swim();
shark.communicate();
dolphin.swim();
dolphin.communicate();
}
}
```

Answer: Both default methods call the same private helper method. The shared steps are written once, which avoids repeating the same code in both methods.Sample Output:Student wakes up and checks the mobile.Personal life activities.Student wakes up and checks the mobile.Professional life activities.

```java
interface Student {
default void personalLife() {
dailyRoutine();
System.out.println("Personal life activities.");
}
default void professionalLife() {
dailyRoutine();
System.out.println("Professional life activities.");
}
private void dailyRoutine() {
System.out.println("Student wakes up and checks the mobile.");
}
}
class Learner implements Student { }
class Main {
public static void main(String[] args) {
Student student = new Learner();
student.personalLife();
student.professionalLife();
}
}
```

Answer: The two public static methods call a common private static helper. The helper remains accessible only within the interface.Sample Output:Common interface logic.First static operation completed.Common interface logic.Second static operation completed.

```java
interface InterfaceUtility {
static void firstOperation() {
commonLogic();
System.out.println("First static operation completed.");
}
static void secondOperation() {
commonLogic();
System.out.println("Second static operation completed.");
}
private static void commonLogic() {
System.out.println("Common interface logic.");
}
}
class Main {
public static void main(String[] args) {
InterfaceUtility.firstOperation();
InterfaceUtility.secondOperation();
}
}
```
